WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.835
Karpathy turned US

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:02.566
data into a

00:00:02.378 --> 00:00:03.227
Civ map

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.259
Andrej Karpathy asked

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:05.919
Claude to fill

00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:07.063
a Civilization style

00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:07.983
game map with

00:00:07.818 --> 00:00:09.080
real United States

00:00:08.892 --> 00:00:09.469
data

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:10.518
and let Opus

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.110
5.5 download and

00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:12.629
parse it

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.399
Seven hours and

00:00:14.211 --> 00:00:15.685
45 thousand lines

00:00:15.497 --> 00:00:16.416
of code later

00:00:16.228 --> 00:00:16.876
it worked

00:00:17.006 --> 00:00:18.315
pulling 31 data

00:00:18.126 --> 00:00:19.411
sources including the

00:00:19.223 --> 00:00:20.779
Census NOAA and

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:21.959
USGS onto a

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.503
25 kilometer hex

00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:23.869
grid

00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:25.329
Built with Claude

00:00:25.141 --> 00:00:25.636
Code

00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:26.556
the result has

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.124
19 interactive lenses

00:00:28.254 --> 00:00:29.209
city views for

00:00:29.021 --> 00:00:31.013
524 metros

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:32.263
and an explorer

00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:33.030
for county level

00:00:32.841 --> 00:00:33.454
data

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.004
Full story on

00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:35.711
the dashboard
